some of these properties look like most private farm yards i have seen, not commercial junk yards.  Over a few decades, vehicles do break down and some farmers (or people in general) just keep them for parts.
e.g., 11920-podzemny-rd-amarillo-tx-79118; 506-e-south-ave-buckeye-az-85326;
I am torn about drones.  From one perspective I think they are excellent tools, on the other i find them extremely intrusive with almost no real recourse.  In the US practically there is little one can do.  Reporting it to the police is waste of time.

Hi, first author here!
I've actually been working on a more approachable blog post introducing the data structure; wasn't expecting to see the paper here first! The repository is [here](
https://github.com/nwtnni/arctic
) and our latest benchmark results are [here](
https://nwtnni.github.io/index-bench/
) (forgive the janky UI). I'm happy to answer any questions--have been quite excited about this work since I believe it's the first time we have a lock-free tree that outperforms lock-based alternatives.

I don't really understand the negative views towards egui in this thread. It works great. In my spare time I've been building an open source little harness thing (
https://www.byob.chat/
) as a fun side project and egui is an absolute blast when it comes to functionality. It so far has behaved as an open canvas, I can press F2, and click and drag any components on my native desktop app to rearrange them, I can also theme it with anything, including live shaders.

This trend drives me nuts! I've bought a VW Multivan T7, second hand, amazing vehicle for my family.
It comes with a set of options you can purchase, for example, extra LED colors for the interiors or Auto headlights, which I find it insane! So you are telling me this vehicle has the tech to auto regulate it's headlights but it sits behind me shelling out +€200 for it? This needs to be made illegal;
Also, having  lock in on where my data goes, effectively needing to pay VW to keep track of my vehicle position or battery status is just crazy; Europe needs to make mandatory all this data to be exposed internally to the user and let him decide what to do with it, either use VW services for convenience or ship it to some third party or self hosted open source service (along with choosing who provides Internet to your vehicle).
